message.content:
Write a home-grown HTML/CSS "section library" for an AI web-builder asset library. Files go in /opt/nxeon-workspace/library/sections/ (directory exists). Do not touch anything else in /opt/nxeon-workspace. No git commits.

Context: Claude (the AI) will copy these snippets into users' sites and adapt them, so they must be excellent, clean, accessible (WCAG 2.2 AA), responsive (no horizontal overflow at 360px), semantic, and look professional/distinctive — NOT the generic "AI SaaS card kit". Read these two files first, they define the contract every section must use:
- /opt/nxeon-workspace/library/base/tokens.css  (CSS custom properties: --color-bg/surface/surface-2/text/muted/border/primary/primary-contrast/accent/success/danger, --font-display/body/mono, --step--1..--step-5, --space-1..--space-10, --section-pad, --container, --radius-*, --shadow-*, --ease, --dur, --measure, --leading-*)
- /opt/nxeon-workspace/library/base/base.css (reset + .container .section .btn .btn--ghost .skip-link .visually-hidden .icon .muted)

Rules for every section file `<kind>-<variant>.html`:
1. First line: an HTML comment header exactly like `<!-- nxeon-section: hero-split | tags: hero split image text cta landing | use: marketing landing pages; one strong image beside the headline -->`.
2. Then the markup (one root element, usually <section class="nx-<id> section"> or <header>/<footer>/<nav>), then ONE <style> block whose selectors are all prefixed with the root class (e.g. `.nx-hero-split ...`) so snippets never collide. Optional small vanilla <script> only where interaction is needed (mobile nav toggle, cart drawer, filter); prefer native <details>/<dialog>. Scripts must be tiny, use no globals except inside an IIFE, and must work when the snippet appears once.
3. Use ONLY the tokens for color/font/space/radius/shadow/motion (no hard-coded hex colors except transparent/currentColor; rgb(from var(--color-...)) or color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-primary) 12%, transparent) is fine). Layout with CSS grid/flex + gap, clamp(), container-friendly; mobile-first media queries.
4. Realistic but obviously replaceable copy (no lorem ipsum): write it for a neutral example business and keep it short. Images: use <img> with width/height/alt/loading="lazy" and src="assets/img/placeholder-<n>.jpg"-style paths (the AI will replace them), or inline SVG shapes. Icons: inline SVG in Lucide style (24 viewBox, stroke="currentColor", stroke-width 2, fill none, aria-hidden="true"). No emoji. No external URLs, no CDNs, no web fonts.
5. Accessibility: landmarks, one logical heading level per section (h2 inside sections; h1 only in heroes), labelled form controls with visible labels, 44px targets, :focus-visible preserved, aria-expanded on toggles, prefers-reduced-motion respected, sufficient contrast with the default tokens.
6. Avoid AI-slop tells: no all-caps eyebrow above every heading, no "01/02/03" markers unless it's a real sequence (timeline/steps), no arrow appended to every CTA, no identical rounded cards with the same soft shadow everywhere, no gradient washes as decoration, no one-accent-word headlines. Vary rhythm: some full-bleed, some split, some dense lists.
7. Keep each file compact (typically 60–160 lines). 

Write these 33 sections (ids = file names without .html):
nav-simple, nav-centered, nav-mega (with mobile toggle each where needed);
hero-split, hero-centered, hero-fullbleed-image, hero-editorial (big type, asymmetric), hero-product (screenshot/device frame), hero-search (input-led, e.g. directory/booking);
features-grid, features-alternating (image/text zigzag), features-list-icons (dense two-column list), features-bento (varied cell sizes, not identical cards);
gallery-masonry (CSS columns), gallery-carousel (scroll-snap, buttons, keyboard accessible);
testimonial-quote (single large quote), testimonial-grid;
pricing-tiers (3 tiers, monthly/yearly toggle optional), pricing-simple (one plan + feature list);
faq (details/summary);
cta-band, cta-split (with email signup form);
footer-simple, footer-columns, footer-big (newsletter + sitemap);
contact-form (name/email/message, client-side validation messages, honeypot);
timeline; stats; team;
product-grid (cards with price, add-to-cart button, filter chips), product-detail (gallery + options + add to cart);
cart-drawer (<dialog>-based, quantity steppers, subtotal; pairs with product-grid via a documented custom event `nx:add-to-cart` with detail {id,name,price});
blog-list, blog-post (article typography: headings, figure, blockquote, code, lists).

Also write /opt/nxeon-workspace/library/sections/index.tsv with a header row `id	kind	tags	use` and one row per section (tab-separated; kind = the prefix before the first dash; tags space-separated lowercase).
Also write /opt/nxeon-workspace/library/sections/_preview.html: a page that links ../base/tokens.css and ../base/base.css and has a <nav> list linking to each section file — just an index, no fetch.

Finally verify: every file has the header comment, every <style> selector is prefixed with the root class, no '#' hex colors inside styles (grep), no 'http' URLs (grep), and HTML is well formed (e.g. run `npx --yes html-validate@9 --config <tmp config extending html-validate:recommended with relaxed rules like no-inline-style off, void-style off, no-trailing-whitespace off>` from /tmp on the files, or a quick parse5-based check; fix real errors). Report the list of files and anything you could not do. Keep your final report short.

